## Outcome and conditions

The retained O001-C2 assessment bank uses P003 as a frozen historical preparation case: its “ready/current” scope statements refer to checked Weeks1–2 in that case. This preserves C4 and every item criterion. P004 additionally teaches checked Week3 through O014–O019; that newer scope is context here and is assessed by those new objectives, not silently added to O001-C2.

Produce a reliable preparation/submission checklist from the supplied course introduction, distinguish confirmed common requirements from unresolved differences, and delimit the academic scope actually prepared.

Required components (all must be elicited and passed):

- C1: Correct 40/20/40 and separate >20 final gate.
- C2: Reliable preparation/submission checklist, with R/reading status.
- C3: Preserves all five unresolved categories without invented resolution.
- C4: Distinguishes the historical Week1 snapshot, historical P003 bounded Week1/Week2 readiness and the larger reported exam scope.

