### Conflicting administrative details

The sources are preserved equally; the table records their differences without selecting a definitive deadline or threshold.

| Detail | Lecture 1 | Syllabus / SIS export | Consequence |
|---|---|---|---|
| Assignment 1 | Announced October 12, deadline October 26 (PDF p. 8) | Announced October 12, deadline October 19 (syllabus PDF p. 1) | The first deadline is unresolved; check the actual assignment instructions or ask the course team. |
| Grade A | 90.5–100 (PDF p. 6) | 91–100 (syllabus PDF p. 2; SIS PDF p. 2) | Integer scores agree, but treatment of fractional totals is not fully specified. |
| Grades B–E | B: 80.5–90; C: 70.5–80; D: 60.5–70; E: 50.5–60 (PDF p. 6) | B: 81–90; C: 71–80; D: 61–70; E: 51–60 (syllabus PDF p. 2; SIS PDF p. 2) | Preserve both sets of boundaries; do not invent a rounding rule or fill the fractional gaps. |
| Fail | 0–50 (PDF p. 6) | 0–50 (syllabus PDF p. 2; SIS PDF p. 2) | Both documents list this range. |
| Week 1 seminar date | Handout header: September 30 / October 1 | Syllabus PDF p. 2 says “Sept 31” / October 1 | September has no 31st; retain this as an apparent syllabus error rather than a usable date. |
| Midterm duration | PDF p. 9 prints “12:30–3:00pm,” also says during lecture time | Syllabus PDF p. 2 confirms November 11 at 12:30, with no end time | The end time is not settled by the uploaded documents. |

