### Boundary of this Week 1 ingestion

The syllabus and SIS export identify Week 1 as unbiasedness, consistency, and efficiency, with Wooldridge Chapters 2 and 5. The lecture asks students to revise cross-sectional OLS assumptions and properties and read Chapter 10 before the next lecture. This is a preparation instruction, not ingested Chapter 10 content. Later-week time series, panel data, instrumental variables, simultaneous equations, and limited-dependent-variable topics appearing in the syllabus are outside this pass. Historical enrollment and pass-rate tables in the SIS export are also excluded because they do not teach a Week 1 concept. [[00_Materials/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Econometrics_II/Week_1/Syllabus_2026.pdf#page=2|Syllabus 2026, PDF p. 2]]; [[00_Materials/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Econometrics_II/Week_1/Předměty.pdf#page=2|SIS export, PDF pp. 2–3]]; [[00_Materials/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Econometrics_II/Week_1/2026_Lecture1_print.pdf#page=13|Lecture 1, PDF pp. 13, 28]]


